<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-section-TransformationsARC" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Effect of transformations on the average rate of change</title>

  <p> Now we formalize the observed relations between the average rate of change of a function <m>f</m> and the average rate of change of each of its respective transformations. </p>

  <p>
    <proposition xml:id="prop-ARCVerticalShift">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>g(x)=f(x)+k</m>, then <md>
            ARC_{[a,b]}(g)=ARC_{[a,b]}(f)
          </md>
          
        </p>
      </statement>
    </proposition>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proof>
      <p>
        Since <m>g</m> is a vertical transformation of <m>f</m>, the <m>x-</m>values are not affected by the transformation. So, we compute the average rate of change of <m>g</m> over the same interval we compute the average rate of change of <m>f</m>. We have 
        <md>
            <mrow>ARC_{[a,b]}(g)= \amp\frac{g(b)-g(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> =\amp\frac{(f(b)+k)-(f(a)+k)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp ARC_{[a,b]}(f) </mrow>
        </md>
        
        </p>
    </proof>
  </p>

<p>
    <proposition xml:id="prop-ARCVerticalDilation">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>g(x)=A\cdot f(x)</m>, then <md>
            ARC_{[a,b]}(g)=A\cdot ARC_{[a,b]}(f)
          </md>
          
        </p>
      </statement>
    </proposition>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proof>
      <p>
        Since <m>g</m> is a vertical transformation of <m>f</m>, the <m>x-</m>values are not affected by the transformation. So, we compute the average rate of change of <m>g</m> over the same interval we compute the average rate of change of <m>f</m>. We have 
        <md>
            <mrow>ARC_{[a,b]}(g)= \amp\frac{g(b)-g(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> =\amp\frac{A\cdot f(b)-A\cdot f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp\frac{A\cdot (f(b)-f(a))}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp A\cdot\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp A\cdot ARC_{[a,b]}(f) </mrow>
        </md>
        
        </p>
    </proof>
  </p>

<p>
    <proposition xml:id="prop-ARCHorizontalShift">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>g(x)=f(x-h)</m>, then <md>
            ARC_{[a+h,b+h]}(g)= ARC_{[a,b]}(f)
          </md>
          
        </p>
      </statement>
    </proposition>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proof>
      <p>
        Since <m>g</m> is a horizontal shift of <m>f</m>, if <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> are <m>x-</m>values for the graph of <m>f</m>, then <m>a+h</m> and <m>b+h</m> are the corresponding <m>x-</m>values on the graph of <m>g</m>. So, if the average rate of change of <m>f</m> is computed on the interval <m>[a,b]</m>, then the corresponding average rate of change of <m>g</m> needs to be computed on the interval <m>[a+h,b+h]</m>. We have 
        <md>
            <mrow>ARC_{[a+h,b+h]}(g)= \amp\frac{g(b+h)-g(a+h)}{(b+h)-(a+h)} </mrow>
            <mrow> =\amp\frac{f((b+h)-h)- f((a+h)-h)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp ARC_{[a,b]}(f) </mrow>
        </md>
        
        </p>
    </proof>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proposition xml:id="prop-ARCHorizontalDilation">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>g(x)=f(Bx)</m>, then <md>
            ARC_{\left[\frac{a}{B},\frac{b}{B}\right]}(g)= B\cdot ARC_{[a,b]}(f)
          </md>
          
        </p>
      </statement>
    </proposition>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proof>
      <p>
        Since <m>g</m> is a horizontal dilation of <m>f</m>, if <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> are <m>x-</m>values for the graph of <m>f</m>, then <m>\frac{a}{B}</m> and <m>\frac{b}{B}</m> are the corresponding <m>x-</m>values on the graph of <m>g</m>. So, if the average rate of change of <m>f</m> is computed on the interval <m>[a,b]</m>, then the corresponding average rate of change of <m>g</m> needs to be computed on the interval <m>\left[\frac{a}{B},\frac{b}{B}\right]</m>. We have 
        <md>
            <mrow>ARC_{\left[\frac{a}{B},\frac{b}{B}\right]}(g)= \amp\frac{g\left(\frac{b}{B}\right)-g\left(\frac{a}{B}\right)}{\frac{b}{B}-\frac{a}{B}} </mrow>
            <mrow> =\amp\frac{f\left(B\left(\frac{b}{B}\right)\right)- f\left(B\left(\frac{a}{B}\right)\right)}{\frac{b-a}{B}} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp B\cdot\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp B\cdot ARC_{[a,b]}(f) </mrow>
        </md>
        
        </p>
    </proof>
  </p>

</section>